{"kind":"reasoning","id":"p2-bf727750","text":"**Defining scope of capabilities**\n\nI need to determine the scope of features based on what the user is asking—there are four substantial capabilities. Notably, I can't utilize external services without user setup. For WhatsApp and email, actual sending would require provider integration, and I couldn’t find WhatsApp in the search.\n\nThe features required are H-36 reminders via WhatsApp, purchase proof via email or WhatsApp, access QR scans, and sharing post-event documents via WhatsApp. I should clarify with the user whether they accept outbound manual links or if they want me to proceed with WhatsApp API integration.**Evaluating integration requirements**\n\nI’m realizing that implementing the Meta API requires specific keys, template IDs, a phone number ID, and business account setup. The user will need onboarding and credentials, and email integration might involve external choices. If I go ahead with the provider abstraction and environment variables, I wonder if those integrations will function correctly without proper API configuration. \n\nBefore implementing anything, it's probably best to clarify which email provider the user prefers. I found no information on WhatsApp from my previous search, so I'll need to look for the official WhatsApp Cloud API and consider using Nodemailer for emails.**Clarifying provider choices**\n\nI need to ask the user about their preferences to choose a provider, specifically between the official Meta WhatsApp Cloud API and an email provider like SMTP. I can also design an entry point for this. \n\nFor features, I should think about implementing a \"provider-adapter\" that requires endpoint credentials without needing to verify actual sends. Creating a direct HTTP fetch to the Meta Graph API makes sense, but I haven't found an existing Nodemailer package. I might lean towards a better email provider service instead. The Knock option adds complexity, but it seems to work for integrating WhatsApp too.**Exploring integration options**\n\nI'm looking into how to offer options via the Meta Cloud API and SMTP for email sending. It sounds like I should research the official WhatsApp messaging API for current information. Maybe I should focus on finding the right stack and provider details through web research. It seems that I need to specify the correct service, as Gravity didn't return WhatsApp provider info. Using existing providers like nodemailer for SMTP might be a practical approach for simplicity.**Identifying email and messaging options**\n\nI’m considering the best outgoing mail provider for SMTP. Using Nodemailer is a viable option, but I need the SMTP host credentials, not tied to a SaaS service. I won't add dependencies unnecessarily. Gravity's recommendation, Knock, seems limited for raw sending, but I can connect through services like SendGrid or Postmark. For WhatsApp, there's the Meta API, but Gravity hasn’t provided a recommendation. I should look up the official documentation online and do some research.","open":false,"collapse":"preview"}
