{"kind":"agent","id":"hd8m0lPSehE","agentType":"researcher-web","displayName":"Web Researcher","prompt":"Verify current official Baileys package/API/docs and WhatsApp Cloud connection behavior for a Node.js Next.js production app as of today. Focus on installation/version, auth state persistence/security, sendMessage text and document URL, connection readiness/reconnect, and any important limits/security cautions. Return official source URLs read and a minimal reliable implementation recommendation.","status":"done","blocks":[{"kind":"tool","id":"hd8xQ2oX0hY","toolName":"web_search","input":{"query":"site:github.com/WhiskeySockets/Baileys README installation useMultiFileAuthState sendMessage connection.update latest Baileys 2026 npm","depth":"standard"}},{"kind":"tool","id":"hd8-b0DZK5A","toolName":"web_search","input":{"query":"site:npmjs.com/package/baileys Baileys package version 7 npm OR site:github.com/WhiskeySockets/Baileys/releases latest release","depth":"standard"}},{"kind":"tool","id":"hd9WyYo1XpQ","toolName":"read_url","input":{"url":"https://github.com/WhiskeySockets/Baileys/blob/master/README.md","max_chars":25000}},{"kind":"tool","id":"hd9WzDlvJVg","toolName":"read_url","input":{"url":"https://www.npmjs.com/package/baileys","max_chars":16000}},{"kind":"tool","id":"hd9W1vmI1N4","toolName":"web_search","input":{"query":"site:developers.facebook.com/docs/whatsapp/cloud-api messages media documents 100 MB templates 24-hour messaging limits","depth":"standard"}},{"kind":"tool","id":"hd9W3yQoIiw","toolName":"web_search","input":{"query":"Baileys officia [… 22,676 characters omitted] `. Meta recommends the uploaded-media ID over a hosted link. The official document docs list supported document formats and a **100 MB** maximum. This `link`/`id` behavior is Cloud API-specific; do not confuse it with Baileys’ `{ document: { url } }` upload input.\n\nCloud API free-form service messages are allowed during the **24-hour customer-service window** after a user messages or calls the business; outside the window, use an approved template. Meta also says to message only users who opted in. Store access tokens server-side; verify webhook POSTs with the `X-Hub-Signature-256` HMAC using the app secret, and deduplicate events because webhook delivery can be retried.\n\nSources: [Meta Cloud API getting started](https://developers.facebook.com/documentation/business-messaging/whatsapp/get-started), [service messages and 24-hour window](https://developers.facebook.com/documentation/business-messaging/whatsapp/messages/send-messages), [document messages](https://developers.facebook.com/documentation/business-messaging/whatsapp/messages/document-messages), [media upload and limits](https://developers.facebook.com/documentation/business-messaging/whatsapp/business-phone-numbers/media), [webhook endpoint verification](https://developers.facebook.com/documentation/business-messaging/whatsapp/webhooks/create-webhook-endpoint/).\n\n### Important cautions\n\nBaileys’ maintainers say the project is **not affiliated with WhatsApp** and discourage spam, bulk automation, and stalkerware. WhatsApp’s Terms prohibit impermissible bulk/automated messaging and unauthorized use, and allow account action for violations. Baileys also depends on a changing WhatsApp Web protocol, so expect breakage and re-authentication risk; it is not the official Cloud API or a supported production messaging contract. For business messaging, Cloud API is the safer default.\n\nSources: [Baileys FAQ](https://baileys.wiki/faq), [WhatsApp Terms of Service](https://www.whatsapp.com/legal/terms-of-service).\n\n**What I could not verify cleanly:** one consistent install/import name for the exact 6.7.16 release, or the exact `fileName` document typing in that release’s version-specific documentation. The date-specific release itself is verifiable; the live Baileys docs are rolling and include newer guidance, so validate those details against the pinned package before shipping."}]}
