{"kind":"agent","id":"hedIAnIYTtw","agentType":"researcher-web","displayName":"Web Researcher","prompt":"As of October 2026, what is the official Baileys package name, stable version and import API for a Node.js TypeScript app? Use official repository and npm/release sources. Confirm documented persistent auth API, socket readiness and QR pairing functions. Return URLs.","status":"done","blocks":[{"kind":"tool","id":"hedV1dmGXTY","toolName":"web_search","input":{"query":"site:github.com/WhiskeySockets/Baileys README npm @whiskeysockets/baileys useMultiFileAuthState connection.update QR pairing code makeWASocket","depth":"standard"}},{"kind":"tool","id":"hedV5jL2juY","toolName":"web_search","input":{"query":"npm @whiskeysockets/baileys latest version releases Baileys official","depth":"standard"}},{"kind":"tool","id":"hedV7tuSvXc","toolName":"web_search","input":{"query":"site:github.com/WhiskeySockets/Baileys/releases Baileys release latest version","depth":"standard"}},{"kind":"tool","id":"hed1cEHPjQA","toolName":"read_url","input":{"url":"https://github.com/WhiskeySockets/Baileys","max_chars":25000}},{"kind":"tool","id":"hed1f2viJaU","toolName":"read_url","input":{"url":"https://github.com/WhiskeySockets/Baileys/blob/master/README.md","max_chars":25000}},{"kind":"tool","id":"hed1layXNu0","toolName":"read_url","input":{"url":"https://www.npmjs.com/package/@whiskeysockets/baileys","max_chars":20000}},{"kind":"tool","id":"hed1qLEv2tc","toolName":"read_url","input":{"url":"https://github.com/WhiskeySockets/Baileys/releases","max_chars":18000}},{"kind":"tool","id": [… 5,077 characters omitted] ting session can reconnect without linking again. The maintainers recommend a database-backed auth store for production; custom stores must also persist key updates.\n\nSocket readiness is reported through `connection.update`: treat `connection === 'open'` as connected. For QR login, render the `qr` value emitted in that event. The current guide says `printQRInTerminal` is deprecated/removed; handle QR rendering yourself.\n\nFor phone-number pairing, call `sock.requestPairingCode(number)` only if the stored credentials are not already registered. The current pairing guide says to use the `qr` event as the trigger—rather than calling immediately after creating the socket, before it is ready. Supply the country code and digits only (no `+`, spaces, parentheses, or hyphens).\n\n```ts\nconst { state, saveCreds } =\n  await useMultiFileAuthState('auth_info_baileys')\n\nconst sock = makeWASocket({ auth: state })\n\nsock.ev.on('creds.update', saveCreds)\n\nsock.ev.on('connection.update', async ({ connection, qr }) => {\n  if (qr && !sock.authState.creds.registered) {\n    const code = await sock.requestPairingCode('15551234567')\n    console.log(code)\n  }\n\n  if (connection === 'open') {\n    console.log('Connected')\n  }\n})\n```\n\nThe example uses pairing-code flow; for QR flow, render `qr` instead of requesting a pairing code.\n\n## Official sources\n\n- [GitHub repository](https://github.com/WhiskeySockets/Baileys) — identifies the project repository and notes v7 breaking changes.\n- [GitHub releases](https://github.com/WhiskeySockets/Baileys/releases) and [v6.7.24 release](https://github.com/WhiskeySockets/Baileys/releases/tag/v6.7.24)\n- [npm package page](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@whiskeysockets/baileys)\n- [npm registry metadata and dist-tags](https://registry.npmjs.org/%40whiskeysockets%2Fbaileys) and [the `latest` package metadata](https://registry.npmjs.org/%40whiskeysockets%2Fbaileys/latest)\n- [Installation and import guide](https://baileys.wiki/installation)\n- [Pairing-code guide](https://baileys.wiki/authentication/pairing-code) and [QR-code guide](https://baileys.wiki/authentication/qr-code)\n- [Socket configuration and auth guidance](https://baileys.wiki/concepts/socket-config)\n- [Auth-state implementation in the repository](https://github.com/WhiskeySockets/Baileys/blob/master/src/Utils/use-multi-file-auth-state.ts)"}]}
{"kind":"reasoning","id":"p8-32b936ce","text":"**Evaluating Baileys architecture**\n\nI'm considering the strong warning about Baileys architecture not handling long-lived sockets reliably in serverless Next.js apps. It seems like this app may benefit from a persistent deployment, as mentioned in the README. I’m thinking I need to check the project execution config and possibly design a singleton socket per request. Also, I must ensure Node is updated beyond version 20 since Baileys requires it. I should install the needed packages and address the dynamic imports as they may affect bundling. Overall, it’s a bit complex!**Analyzing ticket attendee details**\n\nI need to consider whether each ticket attendee has specific details, which could mean sending unique outputs for each participant. The event order may include multiple tickets, so I should check the validity of ticket records. It's necessary to include fields like attendee email and phone, along with event information. I'll also think about deduplicating recipients to avoid sending multiple documents to the same email, while ensuring everything is organized for delivery after payment confirmation.**Considering ticket purchase notifications**\n\nI see that the purchase proof has the wording \"Bukti Pembelian,\" which likely pertains to ticket receipts. I might notify users about ticket issuance based on their call, rather than just on payment confirmation. I should obtain issued QR codes, and the purchase proof could be delivered via email or WhatsApp. The ticket URL can be tied to the buyer’s order number. [… 1,614 characters omitted] endees, the order opt-in would apply to the buyer’s phone instead. It looks like I have to refine some validation processes for the checkout UI.**Planning the Prisma event order**\n\nI'm mapping out the flow for the event order concerning the WhatsApp opt-in feature, starting with the Prisma schema where whatsappOptIn defaults to false. I'll tweak the checkout schema to include t