{"kind":"reasoning","id":"p31-32b936ce","text":"**Deciding on implementation steps**\n\nI need to determine the scope of my implementation right now. I'm considering whether existing changes are ours or linked to the user's earlier work on this task, so I'll want to maintain those. I don't need to change authorization unless necessary, but I need to check the permissions and scope map. There are initial issues with `git diff`, plus ensuring package compatibility with Bailey's installed versions. The user mentioned an API, so I need to establish a connection for QR pairing to access the admin tool. It seems like an extensive scope.**Configuring email and document sharing**\n\nI’m working on configuring SMTP for emailing and found that currently, the documents are uploaded as Google Drive URLs. Instead of attachments, I might just send a URL string to recipients. The existing event documentation URL can be utilized for this, and I’m thinking about sending these links rather than documents. WhatsApp potentially supports sending document link messages, so maybe I could send a text with the URL. I want to ensure I'm targeting paid ticket participants for confirmations and receipts after successful transactions.**Decoupling after settlement**\n\nI’m working on keeping things decoupled after the settlement. I need to search the webhook flow and decide how to store notification rows with category fields, using the existing Notification schema. I'll need to check the status and find the full schema migration. There seems to be a mismatch with WhatsApp in the payment service that I should test. I need to maintain a general queue dispatcher for notifications and create a helper to send messages immediately without durable retries.**Considering event reminders**\n\nI’m thinking about how reminders for events should be sent out before the event starts, not afterward. The status might transition to ONGOING, so there wouldn't be any chance to catch up if they miss it. I need to look at attendee details like phone and email to ensure the correct group is set, and I should notify those with paid orders. Also, each event reminder needs a unique identifier for every order.","open":false,"collapse":"preview"}
